messages:
Alex K: Customer reported a 422 from POST /v1/rerank. They have nested passages inside documents and some passages include a field named "query". Suspect input schema collision. Posting minimal repro below.

Acme Support: Here's the payload we sent: ```json
{
  "query": "how to reset password",
  "documents": [
    {
      "id": "d1",
      "passages": [
        {
          "text": "Reset via Settings > Account > Password",
          "query": "user-facing note used by our generator"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

Emma CS: Thanks — can you paste the full response body too?

Acme Support: Response body: `422 {"error":"AmbiguousQueryError", "detail": "'query' found in nested document/passage and at top-level"}`

Chris Eng: Ok. Quick note: our request unmarshaller expects the top-level "query" (the query text) and treats "documents" / "candidates" as the items to score. If a nested object (passage or candidate metadata) contains a key named "query" we currently attempt to coerce it into the same namespace which can cause a collision and a 422.

Alex K: I tried to repro locally; curl I used:```bash
curl -s -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/rerank \n  -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" \n  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \n  -d '{"query":"how to reset password","documents":[{"id":"d1","passages":[{"text":"Reset via Settings","query":"meta"}]}]}'
```

Raj ML: Root cause summary from inference team: when the parser flattens nested metadata it doesn't namespace reserved keys ("query", "query_text"). That leads to two problems: 1) a server validation error (AmbiguousQueryError) when both exist, and 2) in some cases we silently overwrite the top-level query during feature construction which produces unexpected zero/identical scores. Workarounds: rename nested field (eg "note" or "source_query") or move passage metadata under a "metadata" object that doesn't use reserved key names.

Chris Eng: Short-term working payload example that avoids the collision: ```json
{
  "query": "how to reset password",
  "candidates": [
    {
      "id": "c1",
      "text": "Reset via Settings > Account > Password",
      "metadata": { "note": "generated-from-old-query" }
    }
  ]
}
```

Acme Support: Confirmed — swapping nested "query" to "metadata.note" removed the 422 and we get normal scores. Thanks.

Chris Eng: Filing an internal ticket INF-3421 to address parser namespacing and to add stronger schema validation in the SDKs. Action items: docs update in ~24h to call out reserved keys, SDK patch to reject nested reserved names in ~72h, server-side fix to properly namespace/accept nested fields planned for the next minor release.

Devon Bot: :white_check_mark: INF-3421 created by Chris Eng in repo inference-service. Labels: customer-esc, high-priority. Linked this thread.

Emma CS: I'll follow up with the customer and offer the workaround + ETA for fixes.
